# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, git on Windows checks out with core.autocrlf=true and
# rewrites LF to CRLF in the working tree. That is harmless for source code
# a compiler reads, and fatal for a script a Linux container EXECUTES: the
# kernel reads `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` and looks for an interpreter named
# "bash\r", which does not exist. The failure is
#
#     env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# and it appears only on Windows checkouts, which is exactly the kind of
# bug that survives a green CI run.

# Normalise everything to LF inside the repository.
* text=auto

# ...and keep LF in the WORKING TREE too for anything a container runs or
# parses, regardless of the platform it was checked out on.
*.sh           text eol=lf
Dockerfile     text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile   text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
*.conf         text eol=lf
Makefile       text eol=lf
.env.example   text eol=lf
*.env.example  text eol=lf

# Never touched: eol conversion would corrupt these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ico  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary
*.m4a  binary
*.ogg  binary
